---
// Hero.astro — WorldAgen landing
---
<section id="hero" class="content-section hero-section">
  <div class="title-wrapper">
    <div class="title-with-logo">
      <img src="logo/worldagen.png" alt="WorldAgen logo" class="title-logo" />
      <h1 class="main-title" id="animated-title">WorldAgen</h1>
    </div>
    <p class="title-tagline">Unified State-Action Prediction with Test-Time World Model Training</p>
  </div>

  <p class="venue-badge">🚀 AAAI 2026</p>

  <div class="resources-section">
    <div class="resources-buttons">
      <a href="https://ojs.aaai.org/index.php/AAAI/article/view/38925" class="resource-button" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="resource-icon" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M14 2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8l-6-6z" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"></path>
          <polyline points="14 2 14 8 20 8" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"></polyline>
        </svg>
        <span>Paper</span>
      </a>
      <a href="https://github.com/mll-lab-nu/WorldAgen" class="resource-button" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="resource-icon" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M9 19c-5 1.5-5-2.5-7-3m14 6v-3.87a3.37 3.37 0 0 0-.94-2.61c3.14-.35 6.44-1.54 6.44-7A5.44 5.44 0 0 0 20 4.77 5.07 5.07 0 0 0 19.91 1S18.73.65 16 2.48a13.38 13.38 0 0 0-7 0C6.27.65 5.09 1 5.09 1A5.07 5.07 0 0 0 5 4.77a5.44 5.44 0 0 0-1.5 3.78c0 5.42 3.3 6.61 6.44 7A3.37 3.37 0 0 0 9 18.13V22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"></path>
        </svg>
        <span>Code</span>
      </a>
      <a href="https://huggingface.co/MLL-Lab/worldagen" class="resource-button" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="resource-icon" aria-hidden="true">
          <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"></circle>
          <path d="M8 12s1.5 2 4 2 4-2 4-2" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"></path>
          <circle cx="9" cy="10" r="0.8" fill="currentColor"></circle>
          <circle cx="15" cy="10" r="0.8" fill="currentColor"></circle>
        </svg>
        <span>Models</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="authors-section">
    <div class="authors-list">
      <p class="authors-line">
        Chi Wan<sup class="affiliation-marker">*</sup>,
        Kangrui Wang<sup class="affiliation-marker">*,&dagger;</sup>,
        Yuan Si,
        Pingyue Zhang,
        Manling Li
      </p>
      <p class="affiliations">Northwestern University</p>
      <p class="equal-contribution"><sup>*</sup>Core Contributors&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<sup>&dagger;</sup>Project Lead</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="hero-teaser">
    <img src="figures/teaser.png" alt="Overview of WorldAgen: joint state-action prediction, two-stage test-time training pipeline, and performance gains on CALVIN and LIBERO." />
  </div>

  <div class="hero-abstract">
    <p>
      How can <strong>vision-language-action (VLA)</strong> models adapt to new environments where
      world dynamics shift? Existing methods that combine world modeling with action prediction rely
      on pretraining on static datasets and lack mechanisms for active adaptation at deployment time,
      so they struggle to generalize to unseen object configurations and dynamics.
    </p>
    <p>
      We present <strong>WorldAgen</strong>, a unified framework that jointly learns world modeling
      and action prediction while enabling <strong>Test-Time Training (TTT)</strong>. A shared
      Transformer backbone hosts two heads: a <em>world model head</em> that predicts future states
      from past state-action trajectories, and a <em>policy head</em> that predicts actions conditioned
      on task instructions. A <strong>Mixed Unidirectional Attention Mask</strong> disentangles the two
      heads within a single architecture.
    </p>
    <p>
      At test time, WorldAgen samples exploratory actions, collects ground-truth state transitions, and
      performs lightweight TTT updates to refine its world model. This online adaptation sharpens the
      model's understanding of the environment and, in turn, yields more accurate action predictions —
      delivering consistent gains on <strong>CALVIN</strong> and <strong>LIBERO</strong>.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  /* Stack logo+name on a centered row, tagline on its own centered line below */
  .title-wrapper {
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.6rem;
  }
  .title-with-logo {
    gap: 1.1rem;
  }
  .title-logo {
    height: 128px;
  }
  .main-title {
    font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 6vw, 3.6rem);
  }
  .title-tagline {
    font-size: clamp(0.95rem, 1.7vw, 1.35rem);
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    margin: 0 auto;
    max-width: 760px;
    line-height: 1.4;
    text-align: center;
  }
  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .title-with-logo { flex-direction: row; }
    .title-logo { height: 88px; }
  }
  .venue-badge {
    text-align: center;
    color: #dc2626;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    margin: 0.5rem 0 0;
  }
  .equal-contribution {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .equal-contribution sup { color: var(--accent-color); }
</style>
